From 5e947c1b68ad315359c23ec8ac0b7f806fcc6d9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EQForge <dev@eqforge.local>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:23:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Process audio from the first sample; one-script
 install/update

Three windows let unprocessed audio reach the speakers after playback started:

1. the daemon learned about the graph on a 2 s poll, so a stream that
   WirePlumber had linked to the default sink was re-routed up to 2 s late
   (the reported symptom: 'the first second has no EQ, then it snaps in').
   It now follows PipeWire registry events (pw-dump -m) and reacts in
   ~30-60 ms. New: eqforge/system/watch.py. The poll stays as the safety net.
2. a stream exists on the sink before anyone can move it, so
   'eqforge system always-on on' writes a WirePlumber node.rules drop-in that
   creates new playback streams on EQForge's inputs. New:
   eqforge/system/always_on.py, with guard rails (live node required, only
   Stream/Output/Audio matched, old WirePlumber refused).
3. a node or host started before active-dsp.json existed ran as pass-through
   until the next config poll: the SPA node now builds its chain at node
   creation and polls a missing config 10x/s, eqforge-rt retries ~5x/s.

Also: eqforge status reports the watch channel and always-on state;
scripts/eqforge-update.sh installs and updates from GitHub with a private
venv, versioned sources, native backup, --check/--rollback/--uninstall and
service handling; core/Makefile tracks header dependencies; docs + tests.

Version 1.1.0.
